    "title": "Location & Health Data Notice",
    "updated": "17 September 2026",
    "body": "## 1. Precise location\n\nCRW+ uses precise location to track active workouts, calculate route, distance, pace, and related statistics. CRW+ does not intend to continuously track your location when no workout is active.\n\n## 2. Route storage\n\nWorkout routes may be stored on CRW+ servers to provide workout history and social features. Where the local-only option is available and enabled, route data is kept on the device instead of being uploaded to CRW+ servers.\n\n## 3. Visibility\n\nUsers can use available privacy controls to hide workouts or limit visibility, including friends-only visibility where supported. Before sharing a route publicly, consider whether it may reveal your home, workplace, school, or other sensitive location.\n\n## 4. Apple Health / HealthKit and Health Connect\n\nIntegration is optional. CRW+ may request access to workouts, heart rate, steps, calories, distance, and other fitness-related data needed for a user-facing CRW+ feature. CRW+ does not intentionally request sleep or menstrual-cycle data.\n\n## 5. No advertising use\n\nCRW+ does not sell health or fitness integration data and does not use such data for targeted advertising or marketing profiles.\n\n## 6. User control\n\nYou can decline or revoke location and health permissions through your device settings. Some CRW+ features will not work correctly without the permissions they require.\n\n## 7. Accuracy\n\nGPS, wearable, phone sensor, HealthKit, and Health Connect data may be delayed, incomplete, or inaccurate. CRW+ should not be used as a medical measurement device."
